<%--
Dn_Grand - the farthest <Define> in a three-level extends= chain
(Dn_Child extends Dn_Parent extends Dn_Grand). Every non-class key it sets is also set by
a nearer <Define>, which must override it.

data-mode is the arg case: a data- attribute on a <Define> lands in defaultAttributes and
so in this.args. ($mode on a <Define> compiles to defineArgs instead - see README and
tests/define_args_inherited.)
--%>
<Define:Dn_Grand title="grand" tabindex="-3" data-mode="grand"
    style="color: red; margin: 1px" class="g1 shared">
  <div class="dn-body">grand body</div>
</Define:Dn_Grand>
